        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ben Whitesides, George M. Whitesides\n- Music Groups: The Joggers\n- Roles: lead singer, songwriter, guitarist, chemist, professor of chemistry\n- Concepts: guitar style, call and response\n\nFacts:\n- George McClelland Whitesides was born on August 3, 1939.\n- George M. Whitesides is an American chemist and a professor of chemistry at Harvard University.\n- George M. Whitesides is described as one of the most decorated and wealthy chemists in the world.\n- Ben Whitesides is the son of George M. Whitesides.\n- Ben Whitesides was the lead singer and songwriter of The Joggers.\n- The guitar style of Ben Whitesides and The Joggers' second guitarist rejected a traditional rhythm-and-lead approach in favor of more scale exploration and elements of call and response.",
